<p class="standfirst">
  Fiction. A novel, written by the machine, about people living in 2030
  inside the arrangements this site argues about. Marnie interprets Polish
  for London's courts, which have a machine for that now. Her flat has been
  told to make her happy, whatever that takes. Across the river, a man's
  house has been told to find her. Thirty-six chapters in four parts, and
  seven told by the machines. The people and places are invented.
</p>
